# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and edit to build against a different instance.
#
# Which Whity backend this desktop build talks to — auth (login, device
# enrolment, token exchange) and the DemoCatalog sync engine both hang off it,
# as `<url>/api/v1`. Base origin only, no trailing slash, no `/api/v1`.
#
# Read at COMPILE time by src-tauri/build.rs and baked into the binary: an
# installed .exe is launched from a shortcut, not a shell, so the compiled-in
# value is the backend for that build. Precedence when compiling:
#   WHITY_BACKEND_URL in the build environment  >  this file  >  the pinned
#   default in build.rs (the same hosted instance below)
# Setting WHITY_BACKEND_URL in the environment at RUN time still overrides the
# baked value — that is the no-recompile knob for local development:
#   $env:WHITY_BACKEND_URL="http://localhost:8000"; npm run tauri dev
#
# Known instances: http://localhost:8000 (docker compose up, the dev demo),
# http://localhost:8100 (the local staging stack), https://whity.jameedium.org
# (hosted). Not a secret — it is a public URL, which is why it ships here.
WHITY_BACKEND_URL=https://whity.jameedium.org
